  "step1_summary": "- Chief complaint: Sore throat followed by dry cough for ~1 week; associated shortness of breath, wheeze, and chest pain.\n- Symptoms (onset/duration/severity/aggravating/alleviating): Sore throat started ~7 days ago, cough began 1–2 days after sore throat (dry, non-productive). Shortness of breath began ~3–4 days ago, worse with exertion (walking/exercise) but not at rest; patient says it has not prevented usual activities. Some wheeze and some chest pain reported. Fever for first ~3 days, now resolved. Headache intermittent. Appetite decreased but no reported weight loss. Cough not worse at night; no hemoptysis. Symptoms have fluctuated (better/worse) over the week.\n- Past medical history: Patient states 'no' significant past medical history; explicitly denies asthma.\n- Medications/allergies: No current medications. Allergy: peanuts.\n- Family/social history: Mother had lung cancer. Patient reports minimal past smoking ('once or twice in Amsterdam'); no known asbestos exposure. Born in the US, moved to the UK ~12 years ago. Recent travel only to Europe, nothing exotic.\n- Vital signs/exam findings: No vitals recorded. No physical exam findings documented. Patient reports no palpable neck lumps. No rash reported.\n- Labs/imaging: None mentioned.\n- Additional important note: The transcript records a DOB of 9 May 2016 (which would make the patient ~9 years old), but the consultation content (requesting a sick note for work, some phrasing) reads inconsistently with a child — this discrepancy is present in the record and affects risk assessment.",
